# The Clinical Medical Humanities Program at Loyola University of Chicago.

**Authors:** Thomasma, David C., Marshall, Patricia

## Abstract
A medical humanities program emphasizing clinically oriented training is described. The four-year required curriculum, in which students accompany attending physicians on rounds, is taught by faculty representing a wide range of medical and non-medical disciplines. The approach is seen to challenge good teachers and evoke humanities themes from clinical encounters. (MSE)

